## BOM Notes

1. The exact TT motor voltage and power-supply rating should be entered after verifying the motor label or original purchase information.
2. The IRFZ44N may work in the prototype, but it is not the preferred MOSFET for direct logic-level gate drive.
3. The controller and motor must share a common ground.
4. The motor should never be powered through an ATtiny85 I/O pin.
5. Add the flyback diode before long-term operation to protect the MOSFET and microcontroller.
6. The 3D-printed component count depends on the pumpjack model used.
